<div id="2026-08-27-lan-pause-anycubic" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-08-27 — Pause Anycubic LAN connect for the day; two-colour sign 3MF + delete</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Added explicit per-printer "Pause LAN today" / "Resume LAN" controls on the Printer Farm page (/3d/printers). The pause sets a marker in the printer notes (e.g. [LAN_PAUSED:2026-08-27]). Ping (/3d/printer_lan/ping) and future LAN send paths now gate behind the pause or maintenance/offline status and show a clear message. LAN ping form is hidden when paused.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> User requested to pause LAN work on the Anycubic (Kobra 3) for the day while keeping the ability to resume easily. Only the probe/ping exists so far; no job submission implemented yet.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Also completed today.</strong> On-the-fly two-colour 3MF generation from order filament selections (body/text picks now drive render_for_order in SignGenerator, embedding filament_type + filament_color in 3MF object names and &lt;p:metadata&gt; for slicer slots). Gated delete button for extra sign_generator models (owner or admin only; blocks if queued/assigned/printing jobs exist; cleans files + row). Fixed stale worker 404s and link routing. All changes in worktree for 3d site.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Controller/3d.pm</code> (printers action), <code>Controller/PrinterLan.pm</code> (pause gate in ping), <code>root/3d/printers.tt</code> (conditional buttons + LAN_PAUSED UI), <code>Controller/PrinterLan.pm</code>, new changelog entry. No new DB columns (soft marker in notes).</p>
</div>
